  "prediction": "**Deadly Shooting on Las Vegas Strip Leaves Three Dead and Six Injured**\n\nA violent shooting on the Las Vegas Strip early Thursday morning left three people dead and at least six injured. The incident occurred when a black Range Rover opened fire on a Maserati, causing it to crash into a taxi that burst into flames. The taxi driver and passenger were killed, along with the driver of the Maserati. The passenger in the Maserati was shot and taken to the hospital for treatment.\n\nAccording to police, the shooting was sparked by an altercation at a nearby hotel, which spilled onto the streets. The Range Rover and Maserati were seen speeding down Las Vegas Boulevard, with the Range Rover firing gunshots at the Maserati. The Maserati then crashed into the taxi, which exploded in a fireball.\n\nThe Range Rover was last seen heading north from the scene, with police contacting authorities in three neighboring states to be on the lookout for the vehicle. The SUV was described as a four-door vehicle with big black rims and paper dealer plates from out of state.\n\nThe incident has raised concerns about safety on the Las Vegas Strip, which is known for its high level of security. However, police have assured tourists that the area is still safe and that they have made arrests or identified suspects in each of the recent violent incidents.\n\n**Victims Identified**\n\nThe driver of the Maserati, Kenneth Wayne Cherry Jr., 27, was identified as a local resident who was an aspiring rapper. His attorney described him as a \"stand-up guy\" who was loyal and dependable. The taxi driver, Michael Boldon, was identified as a 63-year-old man who had recently moved to Las Vegas to care for his mother.\n\n**Investigation Ongoing**\n\nPolice are still investigating the incident and have collected video from traffic cameras at the intersection. They are also checking whether the shooting might have been sparked by an altercation at a nightclub. The investigation is ongoing, and police are urging anyone with information to come forward.\n\n**Impact on Tourism**\n\nThe shooting has caused disruptions to traffic and tourism in the area, with many tourists facing problems getting around. However, many tourists have expressed confidence in the safety of the area and have continued to enjoy their stay in Las Vegas.\n\n**Recent Violence on the Strip**\n\nThe shooting is the latest in a series of violent incidents on the Las Vegas Strip in recent weeks. Two people were critically wounded in a shooting at a parking garage on February 6, and a tourist was stabbed in an elevator at The Hotel",
